# hub.tsl — both hub legs, aggregator's firehose and PHP error-log ingest and
# hub-control's settings/discovery egress, in one worker. Frontmatter is read
# from the top-level file only, so all three `var` pins below must live here —
# an included file's own frontmatter is skipped.
#
# `is_hub = 1` declares the site a hub, which `<eln:is_hub>` reads; the one in
# `aggregator` counts only where that file is activated on its own.
#
# `num_partitions = 1` does two things at once: it keeps hub-control's
# single-instance control plane single (without it, a hub configured above
# one data partition would mount that plane once per partition), and it means
# every Remote_Source the `spokes` group builds pulls the spoke's
# `firehose.p0` and `sources/php` on one connection, beside the hub's own
# error log. A spoke running more than one partition needs `aggregator` and
# `hub-control` activated as their own topology instead, with
# `num_partitions` matching the spoke's count: there worker p0 carries
# `firehose.p0` plus `sources/php` on one connection per spoke and tails the
# hub's own log, and p1 and up each carry their own firehose partition.
#
# `on_demand_idle = 0` keeps the worker from idling out between ticks, so the
# hub's SSE pulls and its outbound settings/discovery commands stay open
# rather than cold-starting on the next reconcile pass.

var is_hub = 1
var num_partitions = 1
var on_demand_idle = 0

include aggregator
include hub-control

secure
